WEBVTT

00:00:04.618 --> 00:00:06.423
One click to check
Spider Lint runs WCAG rules right in your tab.

00:00:10.393 --> 00:00:14.376
The spider runs to every issue
Next and Back walk it from one failing element to another.

00:00:16.554 --> 00:00:18.167
A fix you can paste
Suggested HTML shows exactly how to repair the element.

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:21.579
Colors that pass
Low contrast? Get the nearest text or background color that meets WCAG.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.949
Ticket, screenshot or report
A Markdown ticket for Jira or GitHub, a cropped screenshot, or one report for the page.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:30.986
Walk the Tab order
Every element the Tab key reaches gets a number on the page, in keyboard order.

00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:41.673
Hear it like a screen reader
Landmarks, headings, links and controls in reading order, with what a screen reader says.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.988
Catch what gets in the way
Missing names, skipped headings and content outside landmarks, each with a fix.

00:00:51.169 --> 00:00:55.310
WCAG 2.0, 2.1 or 2.2
Each version adds its success criteria on top of the ones before.

00:00:55.358 --> 00:00:58.212
All the way to AAA
From the basics to the strictest criteria, plus best practices.

00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:02.398
Fast spider, dark theme
Every option shows a live preview before you pick it.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.146
Dock it to any edge
Float the panel, or dock it so the page moves aside.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:09.869
The page makes room
Docked on the right, the panel never covers what you are checking.

00:01:09.911 --> 00:01:11.731
Settings apply instantly
Change the rules or the layout and the open panel follows, checking again.
